<EzizeLegalLayout title="Refund policy" description="How EZIZE handles unused coin packs, completed pulls, technical failures, duplicate charges, and monthly membership billing." active="refunds">
  <p class="plain-summary"><strong>Plain-English summary:</strong> Unused coin-pack purchases can be reviewed for a refund within 14 days. A coin used for a completed EZ is normally final. If the machine fails and delivers no completed output, the coin should come back. Billing errors and duplicate charges will be investigated.</p>

  <h2>1. Coin-pack purchases</h2>
  <p>You may request a refund of an EZ coin-pack purchase within 14 days of purchase if none of the coins from that purchase have been used. If coins from the pack have been used, the purchase is normally not refundable because part of the digital generation service has been performed.</p>
  <p>Where local law gives you a longer cancellation period or a right that cannot be waived, that law controls. HobFarm may ask for the account email and receipt reference to locate the purchase.</p>

  <h2>2. Completed generations</h2>
  <p>A coin used for a successfully completed EZ is normally final. A generation is complete when EZIZE records the pull and makes the finished high-resolution PNG and receipt available to the account. A subjective dislike of the image, a change of mind, or a later creative decision does not make the generation a technical failure.</p>

  <h2>3. Failed generations</h2>
  <p>If a technical failure prevents EZIZE from delivering a completed output, the service should automatically restore the coin or make a replacement coin available. If that does not happen, contact HobFarm with the account email, approximate time, and any visible failure reference. Do not include a passwordless sign-in link or complete card details.</p>
  <p>A generation that completed but is temporarily unavailable because of a delivery or account display problem may be restored from the generation record instead of refunded. HobFarm will use the recorded status and output record to distinguish a failed pull from a completed one.</p>

  <h2>4. Duplicate and incorrect charges</h2>
  <p>HobFarm will investigate suspected duplicate charges, incorrect amounts, missing purchased coins, and membership grants not supported by the billing record. Confirmed billing errors will be corrected through restored coins, a corrected balance, or a refund to the original payment method, as appropriate.</p>

  <h2>5. Membership cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>You may cancel HobFarm Club to stop future monthly billing and future five-coin grants. Canceling does not remove unused coins or earlier completed EZs. Membership fees already charged are normally not prorated or refunded after the monthly coin grant has been added, except for duplicate or incorrect charges, unauthorized payments supported by the payment investigation, or rights required by applicable law.</p>
  <p>If a membership payment is refunded, reversed, or disputed, any unsupported monthly grant may be removed from the balance. Coins already spent from that unsupported grant may result in an account balance correction or temporary account restriction while the payment is resolved.</p>

  <h2>6. How to request help</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/contact/">HobFarm contact page</a> and choose the closest billing or account topic. Include the EZIZE account email, receipt or payment reference, date, amount, and a short description. Refunds that are approved are sent to the original payment method. Bank and card-network posting times are outside HobFarm's control.</p>
</EzizeLegalLayout>
